  ## 4. Overflow checks — FAIL

  CalcChange is correctly guarded:

  - Negative fees are rejected before arithmetic: internal/txbuilder/txbuilder.go:201.
  - sendSats + feeSats is checked before the sum/subtractions: internal/txbuilder/txbuilder.go:204.
  - Only after those checks is change calculated: internal/txbuilder/txbuilder.go:208.

  QOGEToSatoshis is not fully guarded:

  - The multiplication check is correctly before multiplication: internal/txbuilder/txbuilder.go:164, internal/txbuilder/txbuilder.go:169.
  - But there is no actual check before adding the fractional value: internal/txbuilder/txbuilder.go:183, internal/txbuilder/txbuilder.go:187.
  - The comment’s proof is arithmetically wrong: it changes the permitted maximum from 92,233,720,368 to 92,233,720, dropping three digits: internal/txbuilder/txbuilder.go:184.

  Concrete failing input:

  92233720368.54775808

  The whole-part multiplication fits, but adding 54,775,808 exceeds math.MaxInt64 by one and wraps. The correct guard must be before addition, for example:

  if fracVal > math.MaxInt64-sats {
      return 0, ...
  }

  parseQOGEDecimal repeats this defect: it checks only the whole-part multiplication and performs the fractional addition unchecked: internal/rpcclient/balance.go:39, internal/rpcclient/balance.go:48.

